{
  "id": "rec-009",
  "description": "(0.5.0) Entry envelope consistency known answers (RFC-ACDP-0018 §7, the Envelope consistency rule and the JCS-equality rules of steps 1-3). Executable, consumer-side. Each vector gives a change entry and the evidence the consumer retrieved ('served': lifecycle_event for a lifecycle entry, registry_receipt otherwise) and the expected verdict. Signatures are NOT checked here (RFC-ACDP-0013 §5, RFC-ACDP-0017 §10.3 and RFC-ACDP-0010 §8 cover them, exercised by rec-006); some signature values are placeholders.",
  "tags": [
    "rec",
    "consumer",
    "0.5.0",
    "changes",
    "executable"
  ],
  "applies_to_profiles": [
    "acdp-consumer-recall"
  ],
  "check_order": [
    "recorded_at: equals event_receipt.accepted_at (lifecycle) or registry_receipt.created_at (otherwise), by string equality -> recorded_at_mismatch",
    "context naming: lifecycle: event.ctx_id and event_receipt.ctx_id equal ctx_id; key_revocation: registry_receipt.ctx_id equals ctx_id; superseded: registry_receipt.ctx_id equals superseded_by -> ctx_id_mismatch",
    "superseded only: superseded_by differs from ctx_id -> self_supersession",
    "superseded only: registry_receipt.lineage_id equals lineage_id -> lineage_id_mismatch",
    "served evidence: JCS(entry.event) == JCS(served.lifecycle_event) for lifecycle, JCS(entry.registry_receipt) == JCS(served.registry_receipt) otherwise -> evidence_mismatch"
  ],
  "_note": "The reason tokens are fixture vocabulary for reporting, not wire error codes. An implementation passes when it reaches the same verdict; it SHOULD report the first failing check in check_order.",
